Validate imported headers without reading them again

Validating an import, the median time of each block header reads its
eleven ancestors, each first asked of the target store and then read and
decoded from the import source again. Above the store's tip, where every
imported header lies, the store cannot have them: asking it is a failed
database lookup per ancestor, about 40 million for the 3.6 million headers
of Mutinynet.

Validate now notes the store's tip as it starts (the store is not written
to until validation ends) and asks the store for no ancestor above it, and
it keeps the latest 32 headers of the import source it met, by height, so
that each is read once. The checks and their outcome are upstream's; an
import of Mutinynet's 3.6 million headers takes about 37% less time.

Applies to github.com/lightninglabs/neutrino v0.18.0.

